{title: You crown the year}
{subtitle: Psalms 65:9–13}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] |
| [Ab] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]With awesome deeds of right[Ab]eousness you [Bbsus4]answer us
[Eb]O God of our salva[Ab]tion, the [Bbsus4]hope of all
[Cm]You set the [Gm]mountains in [Ab]place by your [Eb]strength
[Fm7]Girded with might, you [Bbsus4]hold the earth in [Bb]place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You [Eb]care for the [Gm]land and wa[Ab]ter it
You en[Eb]rich it a[Gm]bundantly, yes [Ab]you do
[Cm]The streams [Bb]of God [Ab]are filled with [Eb]water
[Fm7]To provide the [Bb]people with [Eb]grain [Ab][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]You drench its furrows and [Ab]level its [Bb]ridges
[Eb]You soften it with show[Ab]ers and [Bb]bless its growth
[Cm]You crown the [Gm]year with your [Ab]bounty
[Eb]And your [Fm7]paths overflow with a[Bb]bundance
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You [Eb]care for the [Gm]land and wa[Ab]ter it
You en[Eb]rich it a[Gm]bundantly, yes [Ab]you do
[Cm]The streams [Bb]of God [Ab]are filled with [Eb]water
[Fm7]To provide the [Bb]people with [Eb]grain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ebmaj7/D]The [Cm]pastures of the wil[Gm]derness [Ab]over[Eb]flow
[Bb/D]The [Cm]hills are [Gm]robed with [Ab]joy, they [Eb]sing
[Bb/D]The [Cm]meadows are [Gm]clothed with [Ab]flocks
And the [Fm7]valleys are mantled with [Bbsus4][Bb]grain
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They shout for [Gm]joy, [Ab]they break into [Bb]song
[Eb]The hope of [Gm]all the [Ab]ends of the [Eb][Ab]earth [Bb][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
